# Hash Console Mode v1.0: set Console circuitboard Mode from IC via slot set.
# S8 record count (max 8),S9 writes issued,S10 records skipped as unreadable.
# Records S16..S39 as [ConsoleReferenceId,circuitboard slot index,Mode].
# HashType.Prefab=0,HashType.GasLiquid=1. Mode is durable device state, so this
# is commissioning-class: reclaim the housing once every board reads correctly.
# The slot index and the Mode slot logic type need one live observation before
# this is trusted; see docs/DIAGNOSTIC_INPUTS.md and case LG-DIAG-HASHMODE.
poke 0 HASH("DiagnosticHashConsoleMode.v1")
poke 1 1
poke 2 0
Loop:
yield
get r14 db 8
clamp r14 r14 0 8
poke 9 0
poke 10 0
beqz r14 Loop
move r6 0
move r8 0 # writes issued this pass
move r9 0 # records skipped as absent/unsupported
Each:
mul r12 r6 3
add r12 r12 16
get r1 db r12 # Console ReferenceId
add r12 r12 1
get r2 db r12 # circuitboard slot index
add r12 r12 1
get r3 db r12 # desired HashType Mode
add r6 r6 1
blez r1 Skip
bltz r2 Skip
round r2 r2
round r3 r3
# Read back first: an unreadable slot means no board, or no Mode support.
ls r0 r1 r2 Mode
bnan r0 Skip
beq r0 r3 Next
ss r1 r2 Mode r3
add r8 r8 1
j Next
Skip:
add r9 r9 1
Next:
blt r6 r14 Each
poke 9 r8
poke 10 r9
j Loop
